dungeon unless there's a priest defending it.  Given the power of
a co-aligned altar for altar camping as soon as I am XP=5+
I'll go back and convert every unguarded altar I've found so far.

> Btw: What's the advantage of converting altars using unicorns?

Regular corpses might convert the altar depending on your
XP level.  There's a table of outcomes based on the alignment
of the unicorn, the altar and you.  Some of the entries in that
27-entry table are guaranteed altar conversions.  Which leads
to the question:

BTW: What's the disadvantage of converting altars using unicorns?

If you aren't carefull about what result is in what table entry,
the worst case is you convert to the altar's alignment not the
altar converting to your alignment.  Rather than learn the table
I always use non-unicorns to convert altars then only offer
cross-aligned unicorns on co-aligned altars.


